  "prompt": "Build Mailvora's paying retention matrix for the users who signed up from July to December 2025, one row per signup cohort. A user's cohort month is the month of signup_ts, in UTC, and a user counts as paying in a month with at least one payment that was not refunded, by the UTC month of paid_at. Month 0 is the cohort month itself, month 1 the next calendar month, and so on to month 3. Each cell is the percentage of the cohort's users who paid that month, rounded to 1 decimal (12.5 for 12.5%). The as-of date is 5 January 2026: a month that ends after it is not known yet and shows missing, while a month that has ended with no paying user shows 0. Return five columns, in this order: cohort_month (the first day of the month), m0, m1, m2 and m3. Return one row for each cohort month that has signups. Any row order is fine.",
